\DOC ASSUMPTION_STATE_UPDATE_TAC

\TYPE {ASSUMPTION_STATE_UPDATE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
On a goal whose conclusion is an implication from a state-update equation to a
property, it adds, for each assumption describing a component of the pre-update
state, the corresponding assumption about the post-update state.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. It applies to a goal {A ?- u = s ==> t}, where
{u} is a nest of component writes applied to an earlier state and {s} is the
resulting state:
{
   A ?- u = s ==> t
   ================== ASSUMPTION_STATE_UPDATE_TAC
   A, A' ?- u = s ==> t
}
\noindent Here {A'} is a (possibly empty) list of new assumptions obtained by
restating assumptions of {A} with the earlier state replaced by {s}. The
assumptions restated are those whose components are untouched by the writes in
{u}; they may be equations reading registers, flags, or memory
locations/ranges, negated or boolean-valued flag statements, universally
quantified families of such reads, or implications and arithmetic facts whose
subterms mention the state. Assumptions not of this form (side conditions,
non-overlapping facts, {bytes_loaded}, {MAYCHANGE} facts) are left unchanged
and contribute nothing to {A'}.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the tactic was applied only to goals of this
implication-from-state-equation shape, transformed the assumption list only in
the way described, and always yielded a single subgoal.

\ENDDOC
